WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.920
What is Algebra? It's simple. It's all about puzzles.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.100
Here's one for you.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.320
This plus two equals five.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.760
We just have to find the number in this box.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.460
Which number when added to two gives us five?

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:26.940
Simple! It's three. We can say that three plus two equals five.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.540
This thing we see here contains only numbers.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.020
This puzzle can also be asked in a different way,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.020
We can say that x plus two equals five, find 'x'.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.380
We just used a letter in place of the box.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:46.300
These letters are also called as variables.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.760
Sometimes also referred to as the unknown

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.200
since its values is not known to us.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:53.580
This is Algebra.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.780
It deals with variables and unknowns

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.800
and we are expected to find their value.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.640
But why use variables? Why not boxes like these?

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.900
Let's assume there are three unknown numbers.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.000
Using shapes we can write it as a square,

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.160
plus a slant square, plus an empty circle,

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.760
plus four equals seven.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.440
You had to think of different shapes.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.500
Using variables we can write it as

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:26.940
x plus y plus z plus four equals seven.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.140
This was a little more convenient as compared to the previous case.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.460
But what's the real advantage of using variables?

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.220
Read the short story and the question that follows.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.780
Your friend had a few chocolates with him. A bully came across, took away

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.200
five of his chocolates.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:49.840
And then he had just seven chocolates remaining with him.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.100
How many chocolates did he have before the bully came to him?

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.380
This question has '40 words'.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.940
Let's see if it can shorten the question a bit.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.400
Assume your friend had 'x' chocolates with him.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.140
The bully took away five of his chocolates,

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.960
so we subtract five from 'x'.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.820
And after all this your friend was left with seven chocolates.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.500
This entire thing, will then equal seven.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.000
Now all we have to do is find 'x'.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:26.680
This entire question of '40 words' can be written like this.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.020
So yes,

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.460
Algebra makes life simple.

